- Public setup databases.
- Community setup pages.
- Publicly accessible racing forums.
- RSS feeds.
- Publicly accessible setup repositories.
- User-submitted setup URLs.

The research system should collect:

- Circuit.
- Game version.
- Weather.
- Session type.
- Setup values.
- Source URL.
- Date collected.
- Relevant information about the setup.

The research system must compare different sources and identify useful patterns.

IMPORTANT:

Do not pretend to have performed an internet search if no information was retrieved.

Do not invent sources or setup values.

Respect website terms, robots.txt rules and access restrictions. Do not bypass paywalls or access controls.

Do not scrape search engines or websites in prohibited ways.

