## Storage rules

Never use:
- localStorage for permanent data.
- IndexedDB for permanent data.
- Browser storage for permanent setup histories.
- iPhone storage for permanent preferences.
- Local JSON files as the actual user database.

All user data must be retrieved through the backend.

Temporary data in application memory is permitted.

You may cache static application files for performance, but never use an offline cache as the source of truth for user information.

A secure native iOS Keychain entry may be used solely for authentication credentials or refresh tokens when required. It must never contain the actual setup database or personal driving history.

Use secure authentication, password hashing, protected sessions, validation and account-level access controls.

Do not invent insecure authentication implementations.

